# Copy to ops/backup-recipient.txt and put YOUR age public key below.
#
# This is a PUBLIC key. It is not a secret and it belongs in version control -
# that is the whole point. It lets ops/backup.sh encrypt a backup without
# holding any secret itself, so an unattended nightly job needs no credential.
#
# The matching PRIVATE key is what opens a backup. It lives only in your
# password manager. If you lose it you cannot restore, so treat it exactly like
# FILE_ENCRYPTION_KEY.
#
# Generate the pair once:
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.config/age && chmod 700 ~/.config/age
#     age-keygen -o ~/.config/age/docarchive.txt
#     chmod 600 ~/.config/age/docarchive.txt
#
# age-keygen prints "Public key: age1..." - that line goes here, and the file
# it wrote goes into your password manager.

age1replace_this_with_your_own_public_key
